Package: totaljs-https
Version: 1.0.0-1
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Total.js <repository@totaljs.com>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Depends: totaljs-docker-stack (>= 1.0.0), openssl, ca-certificates, libnss3-tools
Homepage: https://www.totaljs.com
Description: Trusted HTTPS for totaljs.developer
 Makes a certificate authority for this machine (its key never leaves the machine)
 and a certificate for totaljs.developer and every *.totaljs.developer, so the
 addresses of the services and of your projects work with https:// and no warning.
 The authority is trusted by the system (curl, git), by Node.js (NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS)
 by Firefox (through its policies) and by Chrome (the store of the person, filled at the start of the session by totaljs-trust-ca). The proxy keeps serving plain http too.
 The command totaljs-https shows the state and renews the certificate.
